.TH RMDIR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove an empty directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int rmdir(const char* " path ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR rmdir ()
removes the directory named by
.IR path .
The directory must be empty.
Use
.BR unlink (3crunch)
to remove non\-directory entries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged; \-1 on failure with
.B errno
set to the positive Linux error number.
.SH ERRORS
Possible errors include
.BR ENOENT ,
.BR ENOTDIR ,
.BR ENOTEMPTY ,
and
.BR EACCES .
Other Linux
.BR rmdir (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (3crunch),
.BR unlink (3crunch),
.BR rmdir (2)
